# Gate-1 fix spec — per-page fix worker

You own ONE page (slug in your prompt) and may edit ONLY its 3 files (docs review, live copy content-reviews/<slug>.md, brief content-briefs/<slug>.md). Read feature-research/oswa-batch1-rework/worker-spec.md (base rules, Q1/Q2 still open) and feature-research/oswa-batch1-rework/gate1-findings.md (reviewer findings). Apply EVERY finding (blocking and non-blocking) that touches your files. Smallest sufficient change.

Canonical rules for the fixes:
- BMI wording everywhere (reviews AND briefs): "BMI 40 or above, or BMI 35–39.9 with at least one major obesity-related condition — always subject to individual clinical assessment." Never imply 40+ needs a comorbidity; never leave a below-35 surgical pathway implied.
- No risk-minimising or comparative replacement text: kill "serious complications are uncommon", "may support recovery" style comparatives — state facts neutrally (complications can occur; risks are discussed individually; keyhole = small incisions, no recovery/pain comparison).
- Every G1/GLP-1/hospital occurrence needs its OWN paste-ready entry: exact source quote + line ref (docs review only) + drop-in replacement or explicit deletion. Hospital mentions → replacement text "[hospital identity to be verified]".
- Cut-lists must be paste-ready: full quoted source passage + exact replacement or "delete entirely" — no bare ranges or conceptual directions.
- One canonical replacement per source block — remove competing/duplicate replacements; cross-reference instead of repeating.
- Live-copy parity convention (match the original 07-10 live copies): NO "Draft L…" line refs, NO file paths (content-briefs/, docs/…) — anchor by the exact quote alone. Docs review keeps line refs. Content otherwise identical.
- Briefs: remove causal outcome-assurance wording ("protects results", "usually improves", "sustains results", "works best", unconditional "attracts a rebate" → "may attract, requirements-dependent").

When done print a 5-line report of what you changed per finding.

