docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/am-i-eligible.md:280:> Weight-related health conditions: a major obesity-related comorbidity is relevant to MBS assessment at BMI 35 or above, but a condition does not create MBS eligibility regardless of BMI. Examples may include type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, obstructive sleep apnoea, severe osteoarthritis, PCOS, fatty liver disease (NAFLD/NASH) and severe acid reflux; your surgeon will assess the full clinical picture.
