docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/am-i-eligible.md:286:> Draft L233-L240: **1. My BMI is around 30; am I too low for weight loss surgery?  **
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/am-i-eligible.md:287:> Not necessarily. A BMI of 30-34 may qualify for a surgical pathway when weight-related health conditions such as type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, or sleep apnoea are present. If surgery is not the right starting point, our medical team can offer meaningful support through medication and dietitian-led care. The only way to know where you stand is a proper assessment.
