content-reviews/am-i-eligible.md:323:> **7. What if I find out surgery is not right for me?** You will not leave without options. If surgery is not the right fit — due to timing, preference, or for clinical reasons — we can discuss medical weight management pathways including GLP-1 medications and dietitian-led programs. Some patients start there and revisit surgery later; others find it is sufficient on its own. The goal is the right outcome for you, whatever form that takes.
content-reviews/am-i-eligible.md:327:> **7. What if I find out surgery is not right for me?** Some people are not suitable for surgery straight away, or may not be suitable at all. Reasons can include a medical condition that makes anaesthetic or surgery too risky, pregnancy, active substance misuse, an untreated eating disorder or difficulty safely following the required aftercare. Your surgeon will explain the assessment and discuss non-surgical options where appropriate.
