+  - Comorbidities relevant to assessment: a major obesity-related comorbidity matters to MBS assessment at BMI 35–39.9, but a condition does not create eligibility below BMI 35. Examples include type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, obstructive sleep apnoea, severe osteoarthritis, PCOS, fatty liver disease (NAFLD/NASH) and severe acid reflux
